      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "287ece2a_2714eb63",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 24
      },
      "lineNbr": 938,
      "author": {
        "id": 1144419
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-09-19T17:00:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately the protocol version is required also to decide the leaf_version that will be inserted (see line 977).",
      "parentUuid": "f3c785d6_db31c627",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 936,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 938,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "4937b9d9fd43371f207ba20cb7aad1dbba5d7c36",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3e04bb38_7a231d14",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 24
      },
      "lineNbr": 938,
      "author": {
        "id": 1160200
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-09-19T17:05:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Trunks and cryptohome shouldn\u0027t really care about the leaf format. They are supposed to treat the leaf like a black box except the unencrypted part which is append only within a major version.\n\nIf they won\u0027t accept the new leaf format, then there are bugs we need to fix on that end. We may need a make_compatible for the response if the new leaf format doesn\u0027t work.",
      "parentUuid": "287ece2a_2714eb63",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 936,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 938,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "4937b9d9fd43371f207ba20cb7aad1dbba5d7c36",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b82f0bf8_3ad93bdf",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 24
      },
      "lineNbr": 938,
      "author": {
        "id": 1144419
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-09-19T17:42:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "JFYI, trunks/cryptohome needs to know the leaf version because it needs to decide if the leaf needs migration or not. Other options for that would be:\n1 - trunks asks pinweaver if the leaf needs migration.\n2 - cryptohome saves (in the vault_keyset) the protocol used when the leaf was created.\n\nThe first option means an extra request to pinweaver at every user authentication. The second means information kept in two places that has to be updated. If is discussed in DD, and we decided to just decode the leaf and check the version.\n\nThe make_compatible function for response seems to allow us to get rid of protocol_version in the insert_leaf. I will try to make it and see how it works.",
      "parentUuid": "3e04bb38_7a231d14",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 936,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 938,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "4937b9d9fd43371f207ba20cb7aad1dbba5d7c36",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "64ecbbcc_8d9e68f6",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 24
      },
      "lineNbr": 938,
      "author": {
        "id": 1160200
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-09-19T17:52:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The current cryptohome behavior doesn\u0027t perform migration, so as long as you only perform migration if the leaf version is less than what you expect it should be OK for future versions. \n\nThe version fields are supposed to remain at the same offset for backwards and forwards compatibility.",
      "parentUuid": "b82f0bf8_3ad93bdf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 936,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 938,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "4937b9d9fd43371f207ba20cb7aad1dbba5d7c36",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9681cbce_08108634",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 24
      },
      "lineNbr": 938,
      "author": {
        "id": 1160200
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-09-19T17:58:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought about this a little more and this does raise somewhat of a problem because if you want to migrate from not using PCR values to using them and Cr50 gives you a new version of the leaf you would need to be able to check whether or not to replace the leaf by reading\nstruct leaf_public_data_t.\n\n+mnissler@chromium.org Do you have an opinion on the cleanest way to handle this?",
      "parentUuid": "64ecbbcc_8d9e68f6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 936,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 938,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "4937b9d9fd43371f207ba20cb7aad1dbba5d7c36",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "192a2fc3_be5fc8b0",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 24
      },
      "lineNbr": 938,
      "author": {
        "id": 1144419
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-09-20T08:19:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No need to read leaf_public_data_t. Please see https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform2/+/1124856, the code in PinweaverLECredentialBackend::NeedsPCRBinding. We parse unimported_leaf_data_t and as you said, the header will not change. And even if it changes in the future, it will change the leaf only after both cryptohome and pinweaver have reached the version that changes it. Because we always will use the protocol version that both can understand.\n\nThese are the possible scenarios for changes:\n1. old cryptohome + old cr50 -\u003e new cryptohome + new cr50 -\u003e migration needed\n2. old cryptohome + old cr50 -\u003e new cryptohome + old cr50 -\u003e no migration\n3. old cryptohome + old cr50 -\u003e old cryptohome + new cr50 -\u003e no migration\n4. old cryptohome + new cr50 -\u003e new cryptohome + new cr50 -\u003e migration needed\n5. new cryptohome + old cr50 -\u003e new cryptohome + new cr50 -\u003e migration needed\n\nThe migration is done ONLY when user authenticates. When we insert the leaf, trunks knows the protocol used and knows the version the leaf is inserted in. No need to parse anything.",
      "parentUuid": "9681cbce_08108634",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 936,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 938,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "4937b9d9fd43371f207ba20cb7aad1dbba5d7c36",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a3ce9174_60c6ed02",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 24
      },
      "lineNbr": 938,
      "author": {
        "id": 1160200
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-09-20T13:42:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I talked with Mattias during our 1-on-1 yesterday and we are in agreement we don\u0027t want the complexity to fall on the side of Cr50 effectively downgrading leaves (by not sending the latest leaf format). This would make it difficult to reason about the security of the Cr50 code in the future.\n\nleaf_public_data_t should move to pinweaver_types.h and trunks utility needs to expose whether or not a leaf is bound to a PCR. Since it has access to pinweaver_types.h it can check the version and pcr bindings as necessary. That way cryptohome just needs to check if a leaf is bound to a PCR using this function to know if it needs to replace a leaf with the PCR bound version.",
      "parentUuid": "192a2fc3_be5fc8b0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 936,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 938,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "4937b9d9fd43371f207ba20cb7aad1dbba5d7c36",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "842289f4_aaff2227",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 24
      },
      "lineNbr": 938,
      "author": {
        "id": 1144419
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-09-28T11:26:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Implemented to have insert leaf 01 even when protocol is 0. Also try_auth migrates the leaf to 01 with empty pcr criteria when protocol 0 is used. Thank you for design corrections.",
      "parentUuid": "a3ce9174_60c6ed02",
